<article class="env-lemma" id="06PF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06PF">Lemma <span data-tag="06PF">78.27.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $G$ be a group algebraic space over $B$. Endow $B$ with the trivial action of $G$. The morphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [B/G] \longrightarrow \mathcal{S}_ B  \]
</div>
  <p> (Lemma <a href="/tag/044R" data-tag="044R">78.20.2</a>) turns $[B/G]$ into a gerbe over $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/06PE" data-tag="06PE">78.27.1</a> as the morphisms $B \to B$ and $B \times _ B G \to B$ are surjective as morphisms of sheaves. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>